{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pushed for review: change 1717 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1717 (commit fa8c25e04b).\n\nFinal local verification, all three fixes in:\n- main tier (CI's invocation, -m 'not integration and not external', -n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300): 12665 passed, 52 skipped, 0 failed.\n- integration tier (run explicitly, since CI's main invocation excludes it): 194 passed, 1 skipped.\n- gates: 13 check_*.py, complexity baseline unchanged, lint, mypy, all five generators zero diff, actionlint + zizmor clean on the new workflow.\n\nRebased onto current main, which had moved 8 commits. Clean rebase, and re-verified on the new base: 57 tests across the six affected modules pass, mypy clean (523 files), complexity baseline clean.\n\nWorth noting what was in those 8 commits: c8a380e24c 'Retry write-side git temp-file faults' — that is the fix for unheedful-custodial-bluebottle, the bug I filed from change 1702's CI triage. Someone picked it up and landed it, which independently confirms the triage: the write-side temp-file ENOENT really was an unretried transient in the shared git seam, not a defect in 1702. My recheck call on that change was correct for the right reason.\n\nWaiting on LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before submit."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786609673066305001,"uuid":"fb030eb2-a769-4cf8-9e2d-2c3b68b2bb89"}